/*
  QuickLinksSection.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 feature view · 0294 · QuickLinksSection (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native
  `QuickLinksSection` resolves (table "QuickLinksSection") lives here with its web
  `t(key, default)` English value. These entries fold into the app
  `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are kept in a
  per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without
  editing the shared catalog.

  The first two groups are the exact keys extracted from the web source
  (features/vehicles/components/vehicle-detail/QuickLinksSection.tsx): the six
  per-link labels the local `quickLinks` array resolves via `t(nav.x, …)`, plus the
  panel title `t(vehicles.detail.quickLinks, 'Quick Links')`. The English values are
  the literal `t()` defaults the source passes. The final group backs the native-only
  chrome — the VoiceOver copy and the loading / empty / error / connectivity states
  the prompt requires — so the Swift sources hold no English literals.
*/

